// Commune with Nature: `BuffKind::Detecting` applied to `SenseKind::Nature`
// -- the same "wide-radius fauna/flora/water summary sense" doc comment on
// `SenseKind::Nature` describes almost verbatim. Reveals every beast/plant
// creature in range as a one-shot flash, exactly like `locate_animals_or_
// plants.ron`, which this spell shares its `SenseKind` with (one variant per
// *presentation family*, not one per spell, per `SenseKind`'s own doc
// comment). Simplified from the D&D original: no terrain-shape/water-body
// readout exists to surface (`SenseKind::Nature`'s own comment: "the terrain
// half... is not an entity reveal"), and no separate "unnatural presence"
// signal exists either -- this is the living-creature half only.
//
// The D&D original's range is "for miles"; scaled down to 450 m, one tier
// above the 300 m the "locate" family and `locate_animals_or_plants.ron`
// use, reflecting this spell's higher level (5th vs. 2nd) and broader
// "commune with the whole region" flavour -- still nowhere near the source
// text's literal distance, the same bounded-spatial-query trade-off
// `locate_animals_or_plants.ron` documents.
//
// Sheet duration is `Instant`; `duration: Some(1.0)` is the same plumbing
// formality `identify.ron` and `locate_animals_or_plants.ron` both use.
SelfBuff(
    buildup_duration: 0.5,
    cast_duration: 0.5,
    recover_duration: 0.3,
    buffs: [
        BuffDesc(
            kind: Detecting,
            data: BuffData(
                strength: 0.0,
                duration: Some(1.0),
                misc_data: Some(Sense(Nature, 450.0, Snapshot)),
            ),
        ),
    ],
    energy_cost: 40,
    enforced_limit: false,
    meta: (
        school: Some(Divination),
        source: Some(Primordial),
        // level 5 spell -> min_level 30, same `level * 6` convention
        // see_invisibility.ron/true_seeing.ron derive from every other
        // shipped spell that sets this field.
        requirements: (min_level: Some(30)),
    ),
)
